try | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9011-E007 | Adopt structured logging convention in TrustyAI services | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9011-E008 | Adopt structured logging convention in notebook-controller | Implementation | Notebooks | Workbenches | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9011-E009 | Adopt structured logging convention in Training Operator | Implementation | Training Operator | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9011-E010 | Document log format and support example queries | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n\nE010's priority is P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception: the strategy\nfrontmatter priority is Major → P1 (overriding HLR-9's P2 label).\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-9011-E001 Logging convention] --> E002[Dashboard adoption]\n    E001 --> E003[KServe controller adoption]\n    E001 --> E004[Serving runtimes adoption]\n    E001 --> E005[DS Pipelines adoption]\n    E001 --> E006[Model Registry adoption]\n    E001 --> E007[TrustyAI adoption]\n    E001 --> E008[Notebooks adoption]\n    E001 --> E009[Training Operator adoption]\n    E002 --> E010[Log format documentation]\n    E003 --> E010\n    E004 --> E010\n    E005 --> E010\n    E006 --> E010\n    E007 --> E010\n    E008 --> E010\n    E009 --> E010\n```\n\nCritical path: E001 → any adoption epic → E010 (length 3).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002..E009 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The convention (JSON schema, required fields, per-language library guidance) is the artifact every adoption builds against; adoptions cannot start until it is published. The strategy explicitly states adoptions are independent of each other once the convention exists, so no adoption→adoption edges. |\n| E001..E009 → E010 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the format and example queries for support scenarios against what was actually built, so it is