hing the naming style of the other owning teams. Verify with\n  the actual docs team before submission.\n- **Component mapping for HLR-1**: the strategy's Affected Components list does\n  not name a component for the convention work itself. It is assigned to the\n  canonical component `Documentation` as the closest match for a published\n  platform-wide convention (a spec/design artifact rather than user docs).\n  Non-obvious mapping, logged here per the component-name constraint.\n- **Serving Runtimes upstream exposure**: serving runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO,\n  Caikit) are third-party upstream projects. If convention conformance cannot\n  be achieved through configuration or midstream patching, upstream\n  contributions may be needed with uncertain timing — see Tiered Delivery.\n- No priority inversions detected: HLR priorities are consistent with scope\n  (P0 convention + highest-traffic user-facing components, P2 Training\n  Operator and docs).\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nThe per-component structure already delivers value incrementally: every\nadoption epic is independent once the convention lands, so each shipped\nadoption improves support case handling on its own. The only potentially\ndependency-gated piece is the serving runtimes adoption (E004): if upstream\n(vLLM / OpenVINO / Caikit) changes are required, it can lag behind the rest of\nthe program without blocking any other epic or the documentation epic (which\ngates on completion but can describe the format and queries for the components\nthat have landed). No separate Tier 1/Tier 2 restructuring is needed beyond\nthis natural per-epic tiering.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32568,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbd4aa4e928738d4","agent_id":"a6288c6523a76e813","session_id":"b44fd475-ac61-4f5f-bd96-ddf2677bf168","uuid":"838a02cd-c937-4f3b-914a-b68995525d61","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:49:08.460Z