{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a167154def93f75b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9011\n3\tepic_count: 10\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9011\n10\t\n11\tAdopt structured JSON logging across RHOAI components.\n12\t\n13\t## Triage\n14\t\n15\tNot below-threshold: the strategy spans seven components and multiple owning\n16\tteams (Dashboard, RHOAI Serving x2 components, RHOAI Pipelines, Model Registry,\n17\tTrustyAI, Workbenches, Distributed Workloads, plus documentation), with HLRs at\n18\tthree priority levels. Not documentation-only: six of the nine HLRs require code\n19\tchanges in components. Full decomposition follows.\n20\t\n21\tThe strategy states open questions: \"None\" — the convention work (HLR-1) is\n22\tprerequisite design and per-component adoptions are mechanical once it lands.\n23\tNo Investigation epics are warranted.\n24\t\n25\t## Epic List\n26\t\n27\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n28\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E001 | Publish platform structured logging convention | Implementation | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E002 | Adopt structured logging convention in Dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E003 | Adopt structured logging convention in KServe controller | Implementation | KServe | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E004 | Adopt structured logging convention in serving runtimes | Implementation | Serving Runtimes | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E005 | Adopt structured logging convention in Data Science Pipelines | Implementation | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E006 | Adopt structured logging convention in Model Registry | Implementation | Model Registry | Model Registry | P1 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E007 | Adopt structured logging convention in TrustyAI services | Implementation | TrustyAI | TrustyAI | P1 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E008 | Adopt structured logging convention in notebook-controller | Implementation | Notebooks | Workbenches | P1 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E009 | Adopt structured logging convention in Training Operator | Implementation | Training Operator | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9011-E010 | Document log format and support example queries | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n39\t\n40\tE010's priority is P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception: the strategy\n41\tfrontmatter priority is Major → P1 (overriding HLR-9's P2 label).\n42\t\n43\t## Dependency DAG\n44\t\n45\t```mermaid\n46\tgraph TD\n47\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9011-E001 Logging convention] --> E002[Dashboard adoption]\n48\t    E001 --> E003[KServe controller adoption]\n49\t    E001 --> E004[Serving runtimes adoption]\n50\t    E001 --> E005[DS Pipelines adoption]\n51\t    E001 --> E006[Model Registry adoption]\n52\t    E001 --> E007[TrustyAI adoption]\n53\t    E001 --> E008[Notebooks adoption]\n54\t    E001 --> E009[Training Operator adoption]\n55\t    E002 --> E010[Log format documentation]\n56\t    E003 --> E010\n57\t    E004 --> E010\n58\t    E005 --> E010\n59\t    E006 --> E010\n60\t    E007 --> E010\n61\t    E008 --> E010\n62\t    E009 --> E010\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\tCritical path: E001 → any adoption epic → E010 (length 3).\n66\t\n67\t## DAG Justification\n68\t\n69\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n70\t|------|------|-----------|\n71\t| E001 → E002..E009 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The convention (JSON schema, required fields, per-language library guidance) is the artifact every adoption builds against; adoptions cannot start until it is published. The strategy explicitly states adoptions are independent of each other once the convention exists, so no adoption→adoption edges. |\n72\t| E001..E009 → E010 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the format and example queries for support scenarios against what was actually built, so it is blocked by every Implementation epic. Per the docs-authoring priority exception these edges do not push E010's priority upstream. |\n73\t\n74\tNo Investigation epics: the strategy's open questions table is empty and its\n75\tunknowns are all resolved by the convention epic itself.\n76\t\n77\tNo onboarding chain: every affected component already exists in the platform\n78\t(architecture context files exist for Dashboard, KServe, Data Science Pipelines,\n79\tModel Registry, TrustyAI, Notebooks, Training Operator; Serving Runtimes is an\n80\texisting canonical component referenced by the KServe architecture context).\n81\tNo repo-onboarding, license-validation, or konflux-onboarding epics are needed.\n82\t\n83\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n84\t\n85\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n86\t|-----|----------|---------|\n87\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E001 |\n88\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E002 |\n89\t| HLR-3 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E003, RHAISTRAT-9011-E004 |\n90\t| HLR-4 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E005 |\n91\t| HLR-5 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E006 |\n92\t| HLR-6 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E007 |\n93\t| HLR-7 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E008 |\n94\t| HLR-8 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E009 |\n95\t| HLR-9 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E010 |\n96\t\n97\tAll nine HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n98\t\n99\tHLR-3 maps to two epics because it spans two distinct canonical components\n100\t(KServe controller and Serving Runtimes) — Rule 1 (different component →\n101\tseparate epics). Both are owned by RHOAI Serving but concern different code\n102\tbases (the controller vs. the model-execution runtimes vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit).\n103\t\n104\t## Health Warnings\n105\t\n106\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n107\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n108\t  non-functional requirements. Teams were derived from\n109\t  `.context/architecture-context/` owning-team fields; acceptance criteria were\n110\t  derived from the HLRs.\n111\t- **Inferred team for Documentation epics**: no architecture context file\n112\t  exists for the Documentation component; the team \"RHOAI Documentation\" is\n113\t  inferred, matching the naming style of the other owning teams. Verify with\n114\t  the actual docs team before submission.\n115\t- **Component mapping for HLR-1**: the strategy's Affected Components list does\n116\t  not name a component for the convention work itself. It is assigned to the\n117\t  canonical component `Documentation` as the closest match for a published\n118\t  platform-wide convention (a spec/design artifact rather than user docs).\n119\t  Non-obvious mapping, logged here per the component-name constraint.\n120\t- **Serving Runtimes upstream exposure**: serving runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO,\n121\t  Caikit) are third-party upstream projects. If convention conformance cannot\n122\t  be achieved through configuration or midstream patching, upstream\n123\t  contributions may be needed with uncertain timing — see Tiered Delivery.\n124\t- No priority inversions detected: HLR priorities are consistent with scope\n125\t  (P0 convention + highest-traffic user-facing components, P2 Training\n126\t  Operator and docs).\n127\t\n128\t## Tiered Delivery\n129\t\n130\tThe per-component structure already delivers value incrementally: every\n131\tadoption epic is independent once the convention lands, so each shipped\n132\tadoption improves support case handling on its own. The only potentially\n133\tdependency-gated piece is the serving runtimes adoption (E004): if upstream\n134\t(vLLM / OpenVINO / Caikit) changes are required, it can lag behind the rest of\n135\tthe program without blocking any other epic or the documentation epic (which\n136\tgates on completion but can describe the format and queries for the components\n137\tthat