e convention exists, so no adoption→adoption edges. |\n74\t| E001..E009 → E010 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the format and example queries for support scenarios against what was actually built, so it is blocked by every Implementation epic. Per the docs-authoring priority exception these edges do not push E010's priority upstream. |\n75\t\n76\tNo Investigation epics: the strategy's open questions table is empty and its\n77\tunknowns are all resolved by the convention epic itself.\n78\t\n79\tNo onboarding chain: every affected component already exists in the platform\n80\t(architecture context files exist for Dashboard, KServe, Data Science Pipelines,\n81\tModel Registry, TrustyAI, Notebooks, Training Operator; Serving Runtimes is an\n82\texisting canonical component referenced by the KServe architecture context).\n83\tNo repo-onboarding, license-validation, or konflux-onboarding epics are needed.\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n86\t\n87\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n88\t|-----|----------|---------|\n89\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E001 |\n90\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E002 |\n91\t| HLR-3 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E003, RHAISTRAT-9011-E004 |\n92\t| HLR-4 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E005 |\n93\t| HLR-5 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E006 |\n94\t| HLR-6 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E007 |\n95\t| HLR-7 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E008 |\n96\t| HLR-8 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E009 |\n97\t| HLR-9 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9011-E010 |\n98\t\n99\tAll nine HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n100\t\n101\tHLR-3 maps to two epics because it spans two distinct canonical components\n102\t(KServe controller and Serving Runtimes) — Rule 1 (different component →\n103\tseparate epics). Both are owned by RHOAI Serving but concern different code\n104\tbases (the controller vs. the model-execution runtimes vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit).\n105\t\n106\t## Health Warnings\n107\t\n108\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n109\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n110\t  non-functional requirements. Teams were derived from\n111\t  `.context/architecture-context/` owning-team fields; acceptance criteria were\n112\t  derived from the HLRs.\n113\t- **Inferred team for Documentation epics**: no architecture context file\n114\t  exists for the Documentation component; the team \"RHOAI Documentation\" is\n115\t  inferred, matching the naming style of the other owning teams. Verify with\n116\t  the actual docs team before submission.\n117\t- **Component mapping for HLR-1**: the strategy's Affected Components list does\n118\t  not name a component for the convention work itself. It is assigned to the\n119\t  canonical component `Documentation` as the closest match for a published\n120\t  platform-wide convention (a spec/design artifact rather than user docs).\n121\t  Non-obvious mapping, logged here per the component-name constraint.\n122\t- **Serving Runtimes upstream exposure**: serving runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO,\n123\t  Caikit) are third-party upstream projects. If convention conformance cannot\n124\t  be achieved through configuration or midstream patching, upstream\n125\t  contributions may be needed with uncertain timing — see Tiered Delivery.\n126\t- No priority inversions detected: HLR priorities are consistent with scope\n127\t  (P0 convention + highest-traffic user-facing components, P2 Training\n128\t  Operator and docs).\n129\t\n130\t## Tiered Delivery\n131\t\n132\tThe per-component structure already delivers value incrementally: every\n133\tadoption epic is independent once the convention lands, so each shipped\n134\tadoption improves support case handling on its own. The only potentially\n135\tdependency-gated piece is the serving runtimes adoption (E004): if upstream\n136\t(vLLM / OpenVINO / Caikit) changes are required, it can lag behind the rest of\n137\tthe program without blocking any other epic or the documentation epic (which\n138\tgates on completion but can describe the format and queries for the components\n139\tthat have landed). No separate Tier 1/Tier 2 restructuring is needed beyond\n140\tthis natural per-epic tiering.\n141\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b14447b3bc3e9c6e","agent_id":"ac627567882e13ab0","session_id":"b44fd475-ac61-4f5f-bd96-ddf2677bf168","uuid":"e75e1295-1095-4560-a8c9-1ea27c3d7cd3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:59:34.321Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d23ae1d83d6e2dc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9011 decomposition"}
